@page "/docs/forms/fluent-validation"

<DocsPage Title="FluentValidation" Description="Build forms in Blazor using EditForm and FluentValidation.">
    <p>
        In this guide, we will take a look at building forms with <a href="https://fluentvalidation.net">FluentValidation</a>. We&apos;ll cover
        building forms with the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component, adding validation rules with FluentValidation, error handling,
        accessibility, and more.
    </p>

    <DocsHeading Title="Demo" />
    <p>
        We are going to build the following form. It has a simple text input and a textarea. On submit, we&apos;ll validate the form data and
        display any errors.
    </p>
    <Callout>
        <strong>Note:</strong> For the purpose of this demo, the controls don&apos;t use browser validation attributes, so you can see how
        validation and errors work. In production code, you can add them as well.
    </Callout>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-demo" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[700px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />

    <DocsHeading Title="Approach" />
    <p>This form leverages Blazor&apos;s built-in forms and FluentValidation&apos;s rules. We&apos;ll build our form using the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component, which gives you <strong>complete flexibility over the markup and styling</strong>.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Uses <code>EditForm</code> and <code>EditContext</code> for form state management.</li>
        <li>A FluentValidation <code>AbstractValidator</code> for the rules, kept apart from the model.</li>
        <li>A small <code>FluentValidationValidator</code> component that connects the validator to the form.</li>
        <li><code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> components for building accessible forms.</li>
    </ul>

    <DocsHeading Title="Anatomy" />
    <p>Here&apos;s a basic example of a form using a value and change handler per control, and the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@AnatomyCode" />

    <DocsHeading Title="Form" />
    <Steps>
        <Step>Install FluentValidation</Step>
        <CliCommandRaw Command="dotnet add package FluentValidation" />
        <Step>Add the validator component</Step>
        <p>
            Blazor ships <code>DataAnnotationsValidator</code> for attributes, but nothing for FluentValidation. This component plays the same
            part: put it inside an <code>EditForm</code> and it runs your validator whenever the form validates.
        </p>
        <ComponentSource Helper="FluentValidationValidator.razor" />
        <Step>Create a form model and its validator</Step>
        <p>We&apos;ll define the shape of our form with a plain class, and its rules with a FluentValidation validator.</p>
        <CodeFigure Code="@ModelCode" Title="BugReportForm.razor" />
        <Step>Set up the form</Step>
        <p>Next, we&apos;ll create an <code>EditContext</code> for the model, add the validator and handle the submit. The form&apos;s fields go inside the <code>EditForm</code>; we&apos;ll build them in the next step. <code>Submit</code> is where you&apos;d use the values: here it shows them in a toast.</p>
        <CodeFigure Code="@SetupCode" Title="BugReportForm.razor" LineNumbers="true" />
        <Step>Build the form</Step>
        <p>
            We can now build the form using the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component. Each control takes its value from the model and writes
            changes back through <code>Change</code>.
        </p>
        <ComponentSource Example="form-fluent-demo" Title="BugReportForm.razor" />
        <Step>Done</Step>
        <p>That&apos;s it. You now have a fully accessible form with client-side validation.</p>
        <p>When you submit the form, the <code>Submit</code> method will be called with the validated form data. If the form data is invalid, Blazor will display the errors next to each field.</p>
    </Steps>

    <DocsHeading Title="Validation" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Client-side Validation" />
    <p>
        <code>FluentValidationValidator</code> runs the validator you give it against the form&apos;s model. When the form is interactive, validation
        runs in the browser&apos;s circuit (or WebAssembly) without a round trip to your API, and the same validator works on the server.
    </p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ValidatorCode" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Validation Modes" />
    <p>Blazor validates the whole model when you call <code>EditContext.Validate()</code> and a single field when you call <code>EditContext.NotifyFieldChanged()</code>. The examples here validate like this:</p>
    <DocsTable>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>On submit</td><td>The first validation runs when the form is submitted, so untouched fields don&apos;t show errors.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>On change, after submit</td><td>Once submitted, the form revalidates on every change, so errors clear as soon as they&apos;re fixed.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </DocsTable>
    <p><code>Change</code> applies an update and, once the form has been submitted, revalidates it:</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ModesCode" />

    <DocsHeading Title="Displaying Errors" />
    <p>
        Display errors next to the field using <code>&lt;FieldError /&gt;</code>. For styling and accessibility, set
        <code>data-invalid</code> on the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component and <code>aria-invalid</code> on the form control.
    </p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ErrorsCode" />
    <p>The attributes have to be the strings <code>"true"</code> and <code>"false"</code>: the styles target <code>data-[invalid=true]</code> and <code>aria-invalid</code>. <code>Errors</code> returns only a field&apos;s first message, like a schema validator would.</p>

    <DocsHeading Title="Working with Different Field Types" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Input" />
    <ul>
        <li>Pass <code>Value</code> and <code>ValueChanged</code> to the <code>&lt;Input /&gt;</code> component.</li>
        <li>To show errors, add the <code>aria-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Input /&gt;</code> component and the <code>data-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component.</li>
    </ul>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-input" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[700px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@InputCode" />

    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Textarea" />
    <ul>
        <li>Pass <code>Value</code> and <code>ValueChanged</code> to the <code>&lt;Textarea /&gt;</code> component. <code>ValueChanged</code> fires on <code>change</code>; use <code>@@oninput</code> for live updates.</li>
        <li>To show errors, add the <code>aria-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Textarea /&gt;</code> component and the <code>data-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component.</li>
    </ul>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-textarea" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[700px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@TextareaCode" />

    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Select" />
    <ul>
        <li>Pass <code>Value</code> and <code>ValueChanged</code> to the <code>&lt;Select /&gt;</code> component.</li>
        <li>To show errors, add the <code>aria-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;SelectTrigger /&gt;</code> component and the <code>data-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component.</li>
    </ul>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-select" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[500px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@SelectCode" />

    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Checkbox" />
    <ul>
        <li>For checkbox arrays, add or remove the item from the list in <code>CheckedChanged</code>.</li>
        <li>To show errors, add the <code>aria-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Checkbox /&gt;</code> component and the <code>data-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component.</li>
        <li>Remember to add <code>data-slot="checkbox-group"</code> to the <code>&lt;FieldGroup /&gt;</code> component for proper styling and spacing.</li>
    </ul>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-checkbox" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[700px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@CheckboxCode" />

    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Radio Group" />
    <ul>
        <li>Pass <code>Value</code> and <code>ValueChanged</code> to the <code>&lt;RadioGroup /&gt;</code> component.</li>
        <li>To show errors, add the <code>aria-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;RadioGroupItem /&gt;</code> component and the <code>data-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component.</li>
    </ul>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-radiogroup" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[700px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@RadioGroupCode" />

    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Switch" />
    <ul>
        <li>Pass <code>Checked</code> and <code>CheckedChanged</code> to the <code>&lt;Switch /&gt;</code> component.</li>
        <li>To show errors, add the <code>aria-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Switch /&gt;</code> component and the <code>data-invalid</code> attribute to the <code>&lt;Field /&gt;</code> component.</li>
    </ul>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-switch" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[500px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@SwitchCode" />

    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Complex Forms" />
    <p>Here is an example of a more complex form with multiple fields and validation.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-complex" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[1300px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />

    <DocsHeading Title="Resetting the Form" />
    <p>
        Replace the model and its <code>EditContext</code> to reset the form to its default values. Key the <code>EditForm</code> on the
        context, so the form and its validator start over with it.
    </p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ResetCode" />

    <DocsHeading Title="Array Fields" />
    <p>
        A list in your model works for dynamic array fields. This is useful when you need to manage a variable number of fields, such as
        multiple email addresses or phone numbers.
    </p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="form-fluent-array" Class="@("sm:[&_.preview]:h-[700px]")" ChromeLessOnMobile="true" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Array Field Structure" />
    <p>Render the list with a <code>@@for</code> loop and key each field on its item. Copy the index and the item into locals: the child content renders after the loop has finished, when <code>index</code> has moved on. The remove button goes at the end of the input group (see <a href="#removing-items">Removing Items</a>).</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ArrayStructureCode" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Adding Items" />
    <p>Add an item to the list. Disable the button when you reach the limit.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ArrayAddCode" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Removing Items" />
    <p>Remove the item from the list. Only show the remove button when there&apos;s more than one item.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ArrayRemoveCode" />
    <DocsHeading Level="3" Title="Array Validation" />
    <p>
        Use <code>RuleForEach</code> to validate each item. The validator component shows an item&apos;s messages next to its input, so
        <code>Errors(() =&gt; email.Address)</code> finds them.
    </p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ArrayValidationCode" />
</DocsPage>

@code {
    private const string AnatomyCode = """
        <EditForm EditContext="_editContext" OnSubmit="Submit">
            <FluentValidationValidator Validator="Validator" />
            <Field data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Title)">
                <FieldLabel for="title">Bug Title</FieldLabel>
                <Input id="title" Value="@_model.Title" ValueChanged="@(value => Change(() => _model.Title = value ?? ""))"
                       aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Title)" placeholder="Login button not working on mobile" autocomplete="off" />
                <FieldDescription>Provide a concise title for your bug report.</FieldDescription>
                <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => _model.Title)" />
            </Field>
        </EditForm>
        """;

    private const string ModelCode = """
        @using FluentValidation

        @code {
            private sealed class BugReport
            {
                public string Title { get; set; } = "";
                public string Description { get; set; } = "";
            }

            private sealed class BugReportValidator : AbstractValidator<BugReport>
            {
                public BugReportValidator()
                {
                    RuleFor(report => report.Title)
                        .MinimumLength(5).WithMessage("Bug title must be at least 5 characters.")
                        .MaximumLength(32).WithMessage("Bug title must be at most 32 characters.");
                    RuleFor(report => report.Description)
                        .MinimumLength(20).WithMessage("Description must be at least 20 characters.")
                        .MaximumLength(100).WithMessage("Description must be at most 100 characters.");
                }
            }
        }
        """;

    private const string SetupCode = """
        @inject ToastManager Toasts

        <EditForm @key="_editContext" id="form-fluent-demo" EditContext="_editContext" OnSubmit="Submit">
            <FluentValidationValidator Validator="Validator" />
            ...
        </EditForm>

        @code {
            private static readonly BugReportValidator Validator = new();

            private BugReport _model = new();
            private EditContext _editContext = null!;
            private bool _submitted;

            protected override void OnInitialized() => _editContext = new EditContext(_model);

            private void Submit()
            {
                _submitted = true;
                if (_editContext.Validate())
                {
                    Toasts.Add(new ToastOptions { Title = "You submitted the following values:", Description = JsonSerializer.Serialize(_model) });
                }
            }
        }
        """;

    private const string ValidatorCode = """
        <EditForm EditContext="_editContext" OnSubmit="Submit">
            <FluentValidationValidator Validator="Validator" />
            ...
        </EditForm>
        """;

    private const string ModesCode = """
        private void Change(Action update)
        {
            update();
            if (_submitted)
            {
                _editContext.Validate();
            }
        }
        """;

    private const string ErrorsCode = """
        <Field data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Email)">
            <FieldLabel for="email">Email</FieldLabel>
            <Input id="email" Type="email" Value="@_model.Email" ValueChanged="@(value => Change(() => _model.Email = value ?? ""))"
                   aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Email)" />
            <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => _model.Email)" />
        </Field>

        @code {
            private IEnumerable<string> Errors(Expression<Func<object>> field) => _editContext.GetValidationMessages(field).Take(1);

            private string Invalid(Expression<Func<object>> field) => Errors(field).Any() ? "true" : "false";
        }
        """;

    private const string InputCode = """
        <Field data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Username)">
            <FieldLabel for="form-fluent-input-username">Username</FieldLabel>
            <Input id="form-fluent-input-username" Value="@_model.Username" ValueChanged="@(value => Change(() => _model.Username = value ?? ""))"
                   aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Username)" placeholder="blazix" autocomplete="username" />
            <FieldDescription>This is your public display name. Must be between 3 and 10 characters. Must only contain letters, numbers, and underscores.</FieldDescription>
            <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => _model.Username)" />
        </Field>
        """;

    private const string TextareaCode = """
        <Field data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.About)">
            <FieldLabel for="form-fluent-textarea-about">More about you</FieldLabel>
            <Textarea id="form-fluent-textarea-about" Value="@_model.About" @oninput="@(e => Change(() => _model.About = e.Value?.ToString() ?? ""))"
                      aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.About)" placeholder="I'm a software engineer..." Class="min-h-[120px]" />
            <FieldDescription>Tell us more about yourself. This will be used to help us personalize your experience.</FieldDescription>
            <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => _model.About)" />
        </Field>
        """;

    private const string SelectCode = """
        <Field Orientation="FieldOrientation.Responsive" data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Language)">
            <FieldContent>
                <FieldLabel for="form-fluent-select-language">Spoken Language</FieldLabel>
                <FieldDescription>For best results, select the language you speak.</FieldDescription>
                <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => _model.Language)" />
            </FieldContent>
            <Select Items="Items" Name="language" Value="@_model.Language" ValueChanged="@(value => Change(() => _model.Language = value ?? ""))">
                <SelectTrigger id="form-fluent-select-language" aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Language)" Class="min-w-[120px]">
                    <SelectValue Placeholder="Select" />
                </SelectTrigger>
                <SelectContent>
                    <SelectGroup>
                        <SelectItem Value="auto">Auto</SelectItem>
                        <SelectSeparator />
                        @foreach (var language in SpokenLanguages)
                        {
                            <SelectItem @key="language.Value" Value="@language.Value">@language.Label</SelectItem>
                        }
                    </SelectGroup>
                </SelectContent>
            </Select>
        </Field>
        """;

    private const string CheckboxCode = """
        <FieldSet data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Tasks)">
            <FieldLegend Variant="FieldLegendVariant.Label">Tasks</FieldLegend>
            <FieldDescription>Get notified when tasks you&apos;ve created have updates.</FieldDescription>
            <FieldGroup data-slot="checkbox-group">
                @foreach (var task in TaskOptions)
                {
                    <Field @key="task.Id" Orientation="FieldOrientation.Horizontal" data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Tasks)">
                        <Checkbox id="@($"form-fluent-checkbox-{task.Id}")" Name="tasks" aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Tasks)"
                                  Checked="@_model.Tasks.Contains(task.Id)" CheckedChanged="@(value => Change(() => ToggleTask(task.Id, value)))" />
                        <FieldLabel for="@($"form-fluent-checkbox-{task.Id}")" Class="font-normal">@task.Label</FieldLabel>
                    </Field>
                }
            </FieldGroup>
        </FieldSet>
        <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => _model.Tasks)" />

        @code {
            private void ToggleTask(string id, bool selected) =>
                _model.Tasks = selected ? [.. _model.Tasks, id] : [.. _model.Tasks.Where(task => task != id)];
        }
        """;

    private const string RadioGroupCode = """
        <FieldSet data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Plan)">
            <FieldLegend>Plan</FieldLegend>
            <FieldDescription>You can upgrade or downgrade your plan at any time.</FieldDescription>
            <RadioGroup Name="plan" Value="@_model.Plan" ValueChanged="@(value => Change(() => _model.Plan = value ?? ""))">
                @foreach (var plan in Plans)
                {
                    <FieldLabel @key="plan.Id" for="@($"form-fluent-radiogroup-{plan.Id}")">
                        <Field Orientation="FieldOrientation.Horizontal" data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Plan)">
                            <FieldContent>
                                <FieldTitle>@plan.Title</FieldTitle>
                                <FieldDescription>@plan.Description</FieldDescription>
                            </FieldContent>
                            <RadioGroupItem Value="@plan.Id" id="@($"form-fluent-radiogroup-{plan.Id}")" aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.Plan)" />
                        </Field>
                    </FieldLabel>
                }
            </RadioGroup>
            <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => _model.Plan)" />
        </FieldSet>
        """;

    private const string SwitchCode = """
        <Field Orientation="FieldOrientation.Horizontal" data-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.TwoFactor)">
            <FieldContent>
                <FieldLabel for="form-fluent-switch-twoFactor">Multi-factor authentication</FieldLabel>
                <FieldDescription>Enable multi-factor authentication to secure your account.</FieldDescription>
                <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => _model.TwoFactor)" />
            </FieldContent>
            <Switch id="form-fluent-switch-twoFactor" Name="twoFactor" Checked="@_model.TwoFactor"
                    CheckedChanged="@(value => Change(() => _model.TwoFactor = value))" aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => _model.TwoFactor)" />
        </Field>
        """;

    private const string ResetCode = """
        <EditForm @key="_editContext" EditContext="_editContext" OnSubmit="Submit">
            ...
        </EditForm>
        <Button Type="button" Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline" @onclick="Reset">Reset</Button>

        @code {
            private void Reset()
            {
                _model = new BugReport();
                _editContext = new EditContext(_model);
                _submitted = false;
            }
        }
        """;

    private const string ArrayStructureCode = """
        <FieldSet Class="gap-4">
            <FieldLegend Variant="FieldLegendVariant.Label">Email Addresses</FieldLegend>
            <FieldDescription>Add up to 5 email addresses where we can contact you.</FieldDescription>
            <FieldGroup Class="gap-4">
                @for (var index = 0; index < _model.Emails.Count; index++)
                {
                    var id = $"form-fluent-array-email-{index}";
                    var email = _model.Emails[index];
                    <Field @key="email" Orientation="FieldOrientation.Horizontal" data-invalid="@Invalid(() => email.Address)">
                        <FieldContent>
                            <InputGroup>
                                <InputGroupInput id="@id" Type="email" Value="@email.Address"
                                                 ValueChanged="@(value => Change(() => email.Address = value ?? ""))"
                                                 aria-invalid="@Invalid(() => email.Address)" placeholder="name@example.com" />
                            </InputGroup>
                            <FieldError Errors="@Errors(() => email.Address)" />
                        </FieldContent>
                    </Field>
                }
            </FieldGroup>
        </FieldSet>
        """;

    private const string ArrayAddCode = """
        <Button Type="button" Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline" Size="ButtonSize.Sm"
                @onclick="@(() => Change(() => _model.Emails.Add(new EmailAddress())))" Disabled="@(_model.Emails.Count >= 5)">
            Add Email Address
        </Button>
        """;

    private const string ArrayRemoveCode = """
        @if (_model.Emails.Count > 1)
        {
            <InputGroupAddon Align="InputGroupAddonAlign.InlineEnd">
                <InputGroupButton Type="button" Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost" Size="InputGroupButtonSize.IconXs"
                                  @onclick="@(() => Change(() => _model.Emails.Remove(email)))" aria-label="@($"Remove email {index + 1}")">
                    <svg>...</svg>
                </InputGroupButton>
            </InputGroupAddon>
        }
        """;

    private const string ArrayValidationCode = """
        private sealed class ContactEmailsValidator : AbstractValidator<ContactEmails>
        {
            public ContactEmailsValidator()
            {
                RuleFor(contact => contact.Emails)
                    .NotEmpty().WithMessage("Add at least one email address.")
                    .Must(emails => emails.Count <= 5).WithMessage("You can add up to 5 email addresses.");
                RuleForEach(contact => contact.Emails).ChildRules(email =>
                    email.RuleFor(e => e.Address).EmailAddress().WithMessage("Enter a valid email address."));
            }
        }
        """;
}
